    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0317" n="207" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg207"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60p2/32: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Latvia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Coleman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-04-17T12:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 17,
                                1928—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received April 17—9:20
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>35. Department’s instruction No. 415, February 17, 1927,<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d163-f1"/> regarding proposed commercial treaty with Latvia.</p>
                <p>Full accord now reached with Latvian Government on all points and final draft
                    proposed by Foreign Office ready for signature in Legation’s possession. Request
                    immediate telegraphic authorization to sign.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Coleman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d163-f1" n="47" xml:id="d163-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it transmitted the President’s full power authorizing Minister
                    Coleman to sign the treaty.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
